Third-party notices
===================

pi
--

This software began as a port of the following work, and substantial portions
of it still derive from it — 435 of 524 source files name their counterpart in
their module header:

    pi
    Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
    Copyright (c) 2025 notagentdev
    https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
    Licensed under the MIT License

The port is a translation rather than a reimplementation: module paths, type
and function names, and the decomposition into functions follow the original
where nothing argued against it, so that behaviour can be checked against the
source. What has been added since — the MCP client, atomic file leases, the
minified read and patch tools, the codebase index, goal mode, the remote
session protocol, the local and custom OpenAI-compatible providers — has no
counterpart there.

Bash filter
-----------

The bash filter in `crates/notagent/src/core/bash_filter/` — its 63 declarative
filter definitions, its native post-processors and its system adapters —
derives from the following work:

    RTK (Rust Token Killer)
    Copyright the RTK authors
    https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    Baseline taken at commit 5d32d0736f686b69d1e8b9dc45c007d4eb77a0a2 (0.42.4)

A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is available at
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Changes made in this port: the command-line interface, the process runner, the
streaming and tee layers, the trust store, usage tracking, telemetry, the
session scanner and the editor hook integrations were not carried over. What
remains is a buffered library API with the built-in filter inventory embedded
at compile time, and it does not read filter definitions from the filesystem.
